{
  "summary": "Fixes `test_orphan_inherit_rejection` in `p2p_orphan_handling.py` so getdata checks actually test node behavior. It enforces integer types in `PeerTxRelayer.assert_never_requested`, passes integer transaction hashes from the test, advances mocktime so delayed orphan parent requests can arrive, and switches the parent-relaying peer.",
  "problem": "`assert_never_requested` compares its argument to getdata inv hashes, which are Python integers. The test passed hex strings, causing the equality check `int == str` to always evaluate to `False` and assertions to pass unconditionally even if the node erroneously requested the transactions.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit a3c4ad12e9: 'PeerTxRelayer.assert_never_requested compares the hash of every request received, an int, with its argument, and test_orphan_inherit_rejection passed it hex strings. An int never equals a str, so these checks passed whatever the node requested.'",
    "Author verified that mutating the test scenario to trigger requests caused the old string checks to still pass while the new integer checks properly failed."
  ],
